dx - Transparent UI over Bazel: quality, workflow, and environment commands

Commands:
  audit        run security/license audit over resolved scopes (non-mutating; live Gitleaks plus advisory/vuln/SPDX backends)
  lint         run lint analysis over resolved scopes (mutating by default; --check is non-mutating)
  typecheck    run typecheck analysis over resolved scopes (mutating by default; --check is non-mutating)
  format       check or rewrite formatting over resolved scopes (mutating by default; --check is non-mutating)
  generate     emit/sync BUILD files (Gazelle pipeline; mutating by default; --check validates without writes)
  build        run Bazel build over resolved targets
  test         run Bazel test over resolved targets
  coverage     collect LCOV coverage with optional threshold
  run          build and run runnable targets sequentially (explicit labels/patterns; file/dir scopes need exactly one runnable)
  deploy       build and run a single deployable target
  check        run format+lint+typecheck+generate checks in order (non-mutating)
  fix          apply format+lint+typecheck+generate fixes in order (mutating by default; no rerun, run `dx check` to validate)
  clean        prune unselected managed state, never Bazel outputs unless --bazel (no scopes)
  update       update dependencies per set through qualified resolvers (mutating without confirmation; --check is the preset stale gate)
  bump         widen one declared requirement to a new version (explicit; mutating without confirmation)
  migrate      rewrite breaking changes across releases (upgrade-only; mutating by default; --dry-run plans without writes)
  codegen      collect codegen outputs with atomic commit (mutating managed state)
  env          collect the managed development environment (mutating managed state)
  setup        collect setup outputs with atomic commit (mutating managed state)
  init         scaffold dx into a foreign tree (absent-only; mutating by default)
  new          scaffold a minimal qualified project for one language (absent-only; mutating by default)
  upgrade      one-shot pin+migrate+setup composition with recovery pointer (mutating by default; --dry-run plans without writes)
  hooks        manage Git hooks via hermetic Git (mutating by default)
  status       report workspace and target status
  version      report version and pin drift
  watch        watch for changes and rebuild (local only)
  owners       query owners of files via Bazel query
  deps         query dependencies of targets
  why          explain why a target depends on another
  completion   emit shell completions from the CLI grammar (bash|zsh|fish|powershell; --check verifies without writing)
  docs         build, check, and serve the unified documentation site (non-mutating; --check validates without rendering)
  bazel        forward raw arguments to the Bazel launcher

dx [global-options] <command> [scope ...] [-- bazel-options ...]

Scopes: explicit Bazel labels/patterns (//..., //pkg:target, @repo//...), or workspace-relative files/dirs resolved via Bazel query. Graph-scope commands select //... when no scope is supplied; other commands follow per-command defaults (see docs/cli/commands/README.md#scope-defaults). --here (--cwd alias) selects the current directory tree instead (//path/...; //... at the root) and cannot be combined with explicit scopes.

Exit codes: 0 success; 2 CLI-detected usage/scope/owner errors; 1 operational failures; Bazel-authoritative commands preserve Bazel's code.

Output: --output text|diff|json (NDJSON machine protocol on stdout, human text otherwise). See docs/cli/cli-contract.md.

Usage: dx [OPTIONS] [COMMAND] [TARGETS]... [-- <BAZEL_OPTIONS>...]

Arguments:
  [COMMAND]
          First positional: the command word (a [`Command`] value so the same grammar feeds parsing, `--help`, and shell completions)
          
          [possible values: audit, lint, typecheck, format, generate, build, test, coverage, run, deploy, check, fix, clean, update, bump, migrate, codegen, env, setup, init, new, upgrade, hooks, status, version, watch, owners, deps, why, completion, docs, bazel]

  [TARGETS]...
          Later positionals: explicit scopes/targets

  [BAZEL_OPTIONS]...
          Everything after the first bare `--`, forwarded verbatim

Options:
      --workspace <WORKSPACE>
          Override upward workspace discovery (find MODULE.bazel)

      --dry-run
          Resolve and summarize the plan without executing workflows/mutations

      --quiet
          Suppress dx operation summaries (tool diagnostics still print)

      --verbose
          Enable structured diagnostics on stderr via tracing. Default stays byte-identical; `--verbose` adds info-level logs. Orthogonal to `--quiet` (summaries vs logs)

      --output <OUTPUT>
          Select concise text, unified patches, or versioned NDJSON events

      --report <REPORT>
          Write a standard report (sarif/junit/lcov) to file or -; repeatable

      --fail-on <FAIL_ON>
          Lowest diagnostic severity that fails quality commands

      --min-coverage <MIN_COVERAGE>
          Required line-coverage percent (coverage only, 0-100)

      --check
          Check mode (quality/version plus `update --check` preset gate; no mutations in check mode)

      --debug
          Use dx_debug config (build/run/test/deploy only; conflicts with --release)

      --release
          Use dx_release config (build/run/test/deploy only; conflicts with --debug)

      --bazel
          Additionally forward `bazel clean` after pruning (clean only)

      --pin <PIN>
          Re-pin to <version> (version only)

      --rollback
          Re-pin the recorded previous release (version only)

      --configured
          Use cquery instead of query (owners/deps/why only)

      --from <FROM>
          Source version for `dx migrate` plus `dx upgrade` (migrate plus upgrade only). See: `docs/cli/commands/new-upgrade.md`

      --to <TO>
          Target version for `dx migrate` plus `dx upgrade` (migrate plus upgrade only). See: `docs/cli/commands/new-upgrade.md`

      --here
          Select the current directory tree instead of `//...` (`--cwd` alias) (audit/lint/typecheck/format/generate/build/test/coverage/check/fix/docs only; `//path/...`, `//...` at the root; cannot be combined with explicit scopes; never implicit: bare invocations in a subdir stay `//...`)
          
          [alias: --cwd]

      --serve
          Preview the last docs build outputs locally (docs only). See: `docs/cli/commands/docs.md`

      --port <PORT>
          Preview port for `dx docs --serve` (docs only; requires `--serve`). See: `docs/cli/commands/docs.md`

      --offline
          Force cache-only operation without network fetches (audit/update/bump only; `--frozen` alias). See: `docs/deploy/offline-bootstrap.md`
          
          [alias: --frozen]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version
